--[[!
@fqxn CFS
@desc
<section aria-label="Card Forge Studio overview">
<div style="padding:1.6rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:16px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--surface-raised),var(--surface));margin-bottom:1.5rem"><p style="margin:0;color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em">CARD FORGE STUDIO · OVERVIEW</p><h2 style="margin:.5rem 0">Card Forge Studio</h2><p style="font-size:1.15rem;margin:0">Bring card data, drawing instructions, and written game material together in one creative workspace.</p></div>
<h3>How it fits into your work</h3><p>Start with a game and a card set. Edit the source values, inspect the processed results, and use Forge to see what the drawing script makes. PNG export turns the artwork into finished image files.</p>
<figure style="margin:1.5rem 0"><figcaption style="font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.8rem">The big picture</figcaption><div role="img" aria-label="Choose a game then Choose a set then Edit and inspect then Preview then Export" style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.7rem"><span style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0">Choose a game</span><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--accent)">→</span><span style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0">Choose a set</span><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--accent)">→</span><span style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0">Edit and inspect</span><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--accent)">→</span><span style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0">Preview</span><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--accent)">→</span><span style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0">Export</span></div></figure>
<h3>Explore the connected parts</h3><p>These topics explain the nearby pieces of the workflow. Follow a card to see the part it plays.</p><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,240px),1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1rem 0">
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)"><a href="#CFS.Classes.Game">Game</a></h3><p style="margin:0">A game is the home for a whole project: its name, shared settings, and collection of card sets.</p></article>
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)"><a href="#CFS.Classes.CardSet">Card Set</a></h3><p style="margin:0">A card set brings together one collection of cards, its dimensions, and the files that describe how those cards look and behave.</p></article>
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)"><a href="#CFS.Windows.BaseData">BaseData</a></h3><p style="margin:0">Base Data is the table of values you actually edit.</p></article>
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)"><a href="#CFS.Windows.FinalData">FinalData</a></h3><p style="margin:0">Final Data shows the results after card values and scripts have been processed.</p></article>
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)"><a href="#CFS.Modules.Forge">Forge</a></h3><p style="margin:0">Forge is the visual workbench that turns selected card data and drawing instructions into artwork.</p></article>
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)"><a href="#CFS.Modules.Exporter">Exporter</a></h3><p style="margin:0">The export coordinator turns a planned batch into finished output files.</p></article>
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)"><a href="#CFS.Windows.Wiki">Wiki</a></h3><p style="margin:0">The Wiki keeps written game material alongside card-making tools.</p></article>
</div>
<aside style="padding:1rem 1.2rem;border-left:4px solid var(--accent);background:var(--surface);border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;margin:1.5rem 0"><strong>Good to know</strong><p style="margin:.4rem 0 0">Overview pages explain the system in everyday terms. The API entries provide the deeper details. Legacy and deferred pages describe their status explicitly.</p></aside>
<p style="color:var(--muted)">Ready for the details? The child entries in the navigation describe individual methods, inputs, and results.</p>
</section>
<h3>What belongs where?</h3><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,240px),1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1rem 0">
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)">The game</h3><p style="margin:0">Shared configuration, environment helpers, styles, and the collection of card sets live at project level.</p></article>
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)">The card set</h3><p style="margin:0">Each collection has its own data, dimensions, drawing scripts, row processor, code columns, and Notes.</p></article>
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)">Your working preferences</h3><p style="margin:0">Guides, canvas colors, and grid appearance help you work; they do not become card artwork.</p></article>
<article style="padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface-raised);min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0 0 .6rem;color:var(--accent)">Two kinds of documentation</h3><p style="margin:0">API Docs describes Studio. Game Docs links to the loaded game’s separate documentation.</p></article>
</div>
!]]
